+      itself).'
+    deliverable: results/experiment_4023_retire_agreement_selector.json
+    result: OK (conductor)
+  - id: exp4024-fifth-game-explore-first
+    title: 'FIFTH ARC-AGI-3 game first-solve via the PROVEN explore-first method (raises games-solved 4->5; monotonic +1 per
+      the Incremental-Progress rule): exp4004 solved a 4th game (su15) with explore-first -- (1) active exploration OBSERVES
+      transitions, (2) induce mechanic + goal predicate from OBSERVED transitions, (3) GAP-4 verifier validates the rule,
+      (4) act. Apply to a NEW non-spatial-planning game from the win-condition survey. Honest no-solve is a complete verdict.'
+    deliverable: results/experiment_4024_fifth_game_explore_first.json
+    result: OK (conductor)
+  - id: exp4025-arcmemo-solve-transfer-v5
+    title: 'ArcMemo SOLVE-transfer v5 (self-learning MANDATE; extends the exp4005 2668->17->14->10-action compounding to .372''s
+      new content): does the SAME concept memory make THIS milestone''s new solves (exp4021 search-layer / exp4024 fifth game)
+      cheaper? Seed the solver with the accumulated concept memory and measure the action-count reduction vs a cold start.'
+    deliverable: results/experiment_4025_arcmemo_solve_transfer_v5.json
+    result: OK (conductor)
+  - id: exp4026-verifier-vs-judge-efficiency
+    title: "EFFICIENCY axis confirmation (north-star \xA75): the model-free GAP-4 verifier (demo-fit + restricted-namespace\
+      \ execution + content-hash match, ~0.11s/task, $0) vs an LLM-judge selecting from the SAME ARC candidate sets -- accuracy\
+      \ parity at what cost ratio? The verifier-as-COMMODITY framing (Deep Think Q1: necessary but zero-margin) makes the\
